From 560b94c9ed3a32094db94469eecc59f0ed7ec411 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:20:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Document that protobuf_generate import dirs belong in
 IMPORT_DIRS.

protobuf_generate() computes the paths of the generated files from
IMPORT_DIRS/APPEND_PATH only. An import directory of the PROTOS passed
through PROTOC_OPTIONS (--proto_path, -I) is forwarded to protoc but
ignored for that computation, which either fails at configure time
("could not find any correct proto include directory") or declares
outputs that protoc never writes, so the files are regenerated on every
build.

Document that import roots belong in IMPORT_DIRS.

Fixes #30162
---
 docs/cmake_protobuf_generate.md | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/cmake_protobuf_generate.md b/docs/cmake_protobuf_generate.md
index 542cf58..3a1c7d1 100644
--- a/docs/cmake_protobuf_generate.md
+++ b/docs/cmake_protobuf_generate.md
@@ -160,7 +160,16 @@ Multi-value arguments:
     if the schema file is `proto/helloworld/helloworld.proto` and the import
     directory `proto/` then the generated files are
     `${PROTOC_OUT_DIR}/helloworld/helloworld.pb.h` and
-    `${PROTOC_OUT_DIR}/helloworld/helloworld.pb.cc`.
+    `${PROTOC_OUT_DIR}/helloworld/helloworld.pb.cc`. Each import directory is
+    passed to protoc as `-I`, so this is also the place for directories that
+    only contain imported schema files.
 -   `GENERATE_EXTENSIONS` — If LANGUAGE is omitted then this must be set to the
     extensions that protoc generates.
--   `PROTOC_OPTIONS` — Additional arguments that are forwarded to protoc.
+-   `PROTOC_OPTIONS` — Additional arguments that are forwarded to protoc. Do
+    not use it to pass the import directory of the `PROTOS` (`--proto_path` or
+    `-I`): it reaches protoc, but `protobuf_generate` does not use it to
+    compute the paths of the generated files. Depending on the layout this
+    either fails at configure time with "could not find any correct proto
+    include directory", or declares outputs that protoc never writes, so the
+    files are regenerated on every build. Use `IMPORT_DIRS` (or `APPEND_PATH`)
+    instead.
